        <mxCell id="zDzkmC1P3IZ_AxIebGVs-86" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;code&gt;CloudFront&lt;/code&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="60" x="-150" y="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zDzkmC1P3IZ_AxIebGVs-88" parent="1" style="outlineConnect=0;gradientColor=none;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;strokeColor=#FF9900;fillColor=none;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontColor=#FF9900;dashed=0;spacingTop=3;" value="&lt;pre dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 153, 0); font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 15px; text-align: center; white-space: normal;&quot;&gt;Specification:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Region: ap-southeast-1 (Singapore)&lt;br&gt;Environment: Production design&lt;br&gt;Cluster Type: Amazon EKS — Managed Node Groups&lt;br&gt;Availability Zones: 3 AZs&lt;br&gt;Cluster Count: 1 regional cluster&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Worker Nodes&lt;br&gt;• Initial baseline: 3 On-Demand worker nodes&lt;br&gt;• Placement: 1 node per AZ&lt;br&gt;• Instance sizing: subject to load testing&lt;br&gt;• Node autoscaling: Cluster Autoscaler&lt;br&gt;• Reserve capacity for an AZ failure&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Application Availability&lt;br&gt;• Critical stateless services: ≥3 replicas&lt;br&gt;• Spread replicas across AZs and nodes&lt;br&gt;• Readiness and liveness probes&lt;br&gt;• Pod Disruption Budgets for maintenance&lt;br&gt;• Rolling deployments with health checks&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scaling&lt;br&gt;• Horizontal Pod Autoscaler for application pods&lt;br&gt;• Scale using CPU and workload metrics&lt;br&gt;• Node autoscaling for pending pods&lt;br&gt;• Validate capacity with one AZ unavailable&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Networking&lt;br&gt;• VPC: 10.0.0.0/16&lt;br&gt;• Worker nodes in private application subnets&lt;br&gt;• Example AZ-a subnet: 10.0.16.0/20&lt;br&gt;• Unique subnet CIDRs in each AZ&lt;br&gt;• Public HTTPS ingress through ALB&lt;br&gt;• EKS API endpoint: private access&lt;br&gt;• Outbound access: NAT and/or VPC endpoints&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Dependencies&lt;br&gt;• RDS PostgreSQL: transactional data&lt;br&gt;• ElastiCache Redis: read cache&lt;br&gt;• Amazon ECR: container images&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Security&lt;br&gt;• ALB protected by AWS WAF&lt;br&gt;• TLS certificate managed by ACM&lt;br&gt;• Application ingress restricted to ALB&lt;br&gt;• Least-privilege workload IAM permissions&lt;br&gt;• Secrets stored in AWS Secrets Manager&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Observability&lt;br&gt;• Application and infrastructure logs&lt;br&gt;• Monitor p99 latency, errors and request rate&lt;br&gt;• Monitor pod health and resource saturation&lt;br&gt;• Alerts for failures and capacity pressure&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Performance Targets&lt;br&gt;• 500 requests/second across scoped APIs&lt;br&gt;• API p99 response time &amp;lt;100 ms&lt;br&gt;• Measurement boundary defined in solution&lt;br&gt;• Targets require load-test validation&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1160" width="540" x="1800" y="-340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
